# virt — virtualization pack (#25, PROPOSAL §14). The libvirt/QEMU stack with
# virt-manager and the UEFI firmware (edk2-ovmf) for UEFI guests. Installed
# ONLINE on demand (official repos via pacman, AUR via paru) — nothing baked or
# stashed (design pivot #42); only this name-list rides in the image as TEXT.
# (distrobox stays BAKED in goodies.list per §7/§14 — it is NOT part of this
# pack. dnsmasq, libvirt's NAT helper, is already in the archiso releng baseline,
# so it is NOT re-declared here — that would be a double-bake the validity lint
# forbids; libvirt finds it already present.)
#
# post-add adds the user to the `libvirt` group via ii_group_add (the
# reversible mirror of ii-post-install's docker-group idiom) so virsh/
# virt-manager work without root, but does NOT auto-enable libvirtd — it prints
# the enable hint (§14: virt services are not auto-up). post-remove removes the
# group membership (the package set + group row are reverted by the engine).
#
# waydroid (Android container) is gated behind
# `iictl pack install virt --with-waydroid` (AUR — pulls a large image stack):
# post-add installs it only when the flag is passed. It is NOT a plain member.
#meta:type virt
libvirt
qemu-full
virt-manager
edk2-ovmf
# waydroid — AUR, behind --with-waydroid (NOT a plain member; installed by the
# post-add hook only when the flag is passed):
#   waydroid
